 "relevance_note": "Single-patient case report of a boy with Danon disease carrying a LAMP2 variant: \"Genetic analysis identified a maternal hemizygous frameshift LAMP2 variant\".",
 "method_note": "Short case-report text (no tables); extracted by hand, JSON assembled with a small script. One in-scope person, labelled 'patient' (rule 5). The mother is implied only by the word 'maternal' and is not otherwise described, so she gets no row; inheritance recorded as 'inherited maternal' from 'a maternal hemizygous frameshift LAMP2 variant' (the paper does not say how the mother was tested). The HCM diagnosis 3 years earlier is recorded as onset text of the HCM feature, not as age at diagnosis of Danon disease (age at Danon diagnosis not stated). '12-year-old' is the age at presentation/report; follow-up was 8 months post-discharge (exact age not stated). Vital status 'alive' rests on the 8-month follow-up statement. 'decreased muscle strength' mapped to the checklist item 'proximal muscle weakness (skeletal myopathy)' although proximal distribution is not stated. 'Biventricular outflow tract obstruction' recorded as one feature; right ventricular hypertrophy is not stated. Supplementary videos not available as text. No contradictions found.",
